          "id": "51e969fb-d0e3-468a-86bc-0214c9653d78",
          "memory": "Alex's tiny three-leaf basil grew to four leaves by September 29, 2026, which User joked was a dollar-a-leaf scam; Alex said he almost cried because it is actually alive.",
          "event": "ADD"
        },
        {
          "id": "8bd86cc6-3bf4-4acb-a79e-01e0a0f19453",
          "memory": "Alex said on September 29, 2026 his windowsill sun ended up being perfect for the basil after worrying about weird sun, and he still waters it with a spoon to avoid drowning it, referencing tablespoon-gate.",
          "event": "ADD"
        },
        {
          "id": "4dbc2083-c4b6-47e6-a3fa-630476867354",
          "memory": "Alex sent his mom the basil keys-comparison photo and FaceTimed next to it around September 29, 2026; she laughed for a full minute saying that is not green stuff in the apartment, with User teasing four leaves is like 3 grams and pesto in 9 years instead of 10.",
          "event": "ADD"
        },
        {
          "id": "1f3791d6-57fa-4f7e-9a4c-ffcf6bd29e40",
          "memory": "On September 29, 2026 User got home around 7:10pm still in work clothes on the floor but said the couch is clear, progress from September 20 when the couch was covered for laundry floor camp; laundry is mostly done except one mystery sock with no match, joked the sock is bigger than the basil.",
          "event": "ADD"
        },
        {
          "id": "b339040a-03d4-456a-beba-c9a638699603",
          "memory": "Alex invited User to pizza at Mario's at 6pm on Saturday, October 3, 2026; User declined because parents planned a family visit that weekend with dinner at their place Saturday, joking about enduring Dad's grill stories and 2-hour burger lecture and preferring Mario's; Alex may do takeout instead and User recommended the garlic knots as elite.",
          "event": "ADD"
